.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt PIEBREW 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm piebrew
.Nd Homebrew bottles installed as dpkg packages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Cm install
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl -reinstall
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -keep-deb
.Op Fl -tag Ar tag
.Ar formula ...
.Nm
.Cm remove Ns | Ns Cm uninstall
.Ar formula ...
.Nm
.Cm list
.Nm
.Cm info
.Ar formula
.Nm
.Cm outdated
.Nm
.Cm upgrade
.Op Fl n
.Op Ar formula ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs programs from Homebrew's arm64 bottles.
It asks Homebrew's API for the formula, fetches its bottle into memory
and checks its SHA-256, and makes a Debian package of it there, without
unpacking anything to disk: the keg in
.Pa /opt/homebrew/Cellar/ Ns Ar formula Ns / Ns Ar version ,
its placeholders relocated as
.Xr brew 1
would, each Mach-O file signed again (ad hoc, with 4 KB pages), and
the symlinks
.Cm brew link
makes in
.Pa /opt/homebrew/bin ,
.Pa lib ,
.Pa share
and the others (none for a keg-only formula), and
.Pa /opt/homebrew/opt/ Ns Ar formula .
The package is named
.Sy brew- Ns Ar formula
and is installed with
.Xr dpkg 1 ,
so dpkg and apt list it, remove it and replace it with a newer version;
it depends on the
.Sy brew-
packages of the formula's dependencies, which
.Nm
installs first (marked as installed automatically, for
.Cm apt autoremove ) ,
and on the system packages owning the libraries it loads.
The files keep the names they have in the bottle.
.Bl -tag -width outdated
.It Cm install
Install each
.Ar formula ,
or replace an installed one with a newer bottle.
.It Cm remove , Cm uninstall
Remove the packages of the formulae
.Pq Cm dpkg -r .
.It Cm list
The installed formulae, their package versions and names.
.It Cm info
What the API says of
.Ar formula ,
and whether it is installed.
.It Cm outdated
The installed formulae the API has a newer bottle of.
.It Cm upgrade
Install those newer bottles (of the formulae given, or of all).
.El
.Pp
Options:
.Bl -tag -width "--keep-deb"
.It Fl n , Fl -dry-run
Make the package in
.Pa /var/cache/piebrew
and do not install it.
.It Fl -reinstall
Install even if the same version is installed.
.It Fl -force
Install a bottle that loads a library this system does not have.
.It Fl -keep-deb
Keep the package in
.Pa /var/cache/piebrew .
.It Fl -tag Ar tag
Pour the bottle of this tag
.Pq default: the newest of arm64_tahoe, arm64_sequoia, ..., all .
.It Fl v
Say what is fetched and run.
.El
.Pp
A system library a bottle's file loads that this system does not have
is weak-linked, with a warning, if the file imports nothing from it:
programs built with gnulib (libunistring, gettext, ...) link CoreServices
only for Apple's CoreFoundation's sake.
Otherwise such a bottle is refused, unless
.Fl -force .
.Pp
Post-install steps (Ruby code in a formula) are not run; a formula that
has one is named.
Add
.Pa /opt/homebrew/bin
to
.Ev PATH .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PIEBREW_BOTTLES
.It Ev PIEBREW_API
The API's base URL (default https://formulae.brew.sh/api).
.It Ev PIEBREW_BOTTLES
Fetch bottles from this URL in place of https://ghcr.io/v2/.
.It Ev PIEBREW_CACHE
In place of
.Pa /var/cache/piebrew .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl piebrew install htop
.Dl piebrew list
.Dl dpkg -L brew-htop
.Dl piebrew upgrade
.Dl piebrew remove htop && apt-get autoremove
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr apt-get 8 ,
.Xr dpkg 1
